{
  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5547",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to have a complex relationship with HEC-1, as it is a target of multiple pathways that ultimately lead to HEC-1. The first pathway links Mollicellin N to A704, which is then targeted by palmarumycin CP18, and finally, palmarumycin CP18 targets HEC-1. In another pathway, Mollicellin N directly targets Leukocyte common antigen, which is subsequently targeted by 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which also targets HEC-1. These two distinct pathways provide converging evidence that Mollicellin N influences HEC-1 through different molecular intermediates. The integration of these pathways suggests that Mollicellin N may act as a modulator of HEC-1 through multiple mechanisms, potentially by affecting the expression or activity of downstream targets. The shared involvement of HEC-1 in both pathways highlights the importance of this cell type in the biological response to Mollicellin N.",
